    "description": "Shorten the project lead skill to under 500 lines\n\n## Summary\n\nThe project lead skill had grown to 565 lines, over its 500-line target, and it loads into every project-lead run. This change moves two parts that only some runs need into their own reference files: the rules for a run that an orchestrator started, and the rules for a resumed run. It also removes two passages that repeated a rule another file already owns. The skill is now 488 lines, and a project lead takes the same steps as before.\n\nCloses #163\n\n**Ticket:** [#163](https://github.com/jerridan/crew/issues/163)\n**Type:** Refactor\n\n---\n\n## Agent context\n\n### Authority\n\n- `skills/project-lead/references/writing-standard.md` \"Size\": the 500-line target of a `SKILL.md` body.\n- `CLAUDE.md` \"Authority\": a rule lives in exactly one file.\n- `docs/design.md` §15.146 records this change; §15.20d, §15.89e and §12 are why no sub-skill was used.\n\n### What changed, by file\n\n- `skills/project-lead/SKILL.md`: \"Report to an orchestrator\" and the five resume paragraphs of \"Take the goal\" moved out; the default deploy signal paragraph is now a pointer to `pr-watch.md`'s \"Arm the deploy watch\"; the section \"A step the principal replaced\" is removed; two new rows in \"Where the rules live\". 565 to 488 lines.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/orchestrator-report.md`: new. The moved \"Report to an orchestrator\" section, word for word, with a title and an opening paragraph.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/resume.md`: new. The moved resume paragraphs. The bold skip sentence stays in `SKILL.md`. One added sentence sends a resumed run with `run.orchestrator` set to `orchestrator-report.md`, because the moved section was in context on every resume before.\n- `skills/project-lead/references/autonomy-contract.md`, `record-format.md`, `simple-path.md`, `skeptical-review.md`: pointers now name the new files.\n- `skills/delivered-window/SKILL.md`, `skills/orchestrator/SKILL.md`, `skills/orchestrator/references/orchestrator-record.md`, `skills/review/SKILL.md`: pointers now name the new files.\n- `CLAUDE.md`: fourteen references; the Authority list names the two new files.\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`: version 0.1.113.\n- `docs/design.md`: entry 146.\n\n### Constraints that applied\n\n- One copy of each rule: the moved text exists only in its new file. The removed deploy paragraph and the removed section were second copies: `pr-watch.md` owns the default deploy signal, and the `substitution.md` row, \"Have the spec reviewed\" and `simple-path.md`'s \"The skeptical review\" route each replaced step.\n- No sub-skill: a teammate does not apply `skills:`, and the `Skill` tool is refused in headless `claude -p`.\n- The version bump: the change touches `skills/`.\n- The repo is public: the diff names no employer, colleague or private repo.\n\n### How this was verified\n\n- `wc -l skills/project-lead/SKILL.md` prints 488.\n- A scan of every file outside `docs/`, with line breaks joined, finds no pointer to \"Report to an orchestrator\", and \"A step the principal replaced\" only as `substitution.md`'s own title. Every quoted `SKILL.md` section name outside `docs/` matches a heading that exists.\n- A spec critic ran two rounds on the plan. A headless skeptical review ran two rounds on the local head before the first push. Round 1 found two pointers broken across lines, a resume that no longer reached the orchestrator rules, and a second copy of the resume skip sentence; all three are fixed. Round 2 was accepted with one nit, which is fixed in the last commit.\n\n### Known gaps\n\nNo run has used the shorter skill yet. PR 165 merges first and can add pointers to the moved parts; this branch is rebased and searched again after it merges.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
